ways kept and carries no key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"When sampling runs","level":3,"anchor":"When-sampling-runs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s worker samples each record after its enrichers, whose keys a sampler can read, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before its consent and its store. So a dropped event is never held, written to disk or delivered."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each drop is reported on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"samplingDropReports"},{"type":"text","text":", merged into one report per event type while unread,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as rejections are."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decisions come from the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"samplingSeed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", drawn from the system’s random number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generator once per tracker unless you pass one. They are the same on every platform and Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"release, so with the seed fixed, which events are kept is fixed too:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let tracker = Tracker(samplers: [.events(of: Scrolled.self, rate: 0.1)], samplingSeed: 42)","for offset in 0 ..< 100 {","    tracker.track(Scrolled(offset: offset))","}","await tracker.finish()","for await report in tracker.samplingDropReports {","    print(report)  \/\/ Scrolled: 89 sampled out","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s decision is made from the seed and the session’s identifier alone, so nothing records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The sampler keeps only the current session’s decision, in memory, and never writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier anywhere. Records that a store recovered from an earlier run were sampled in that run,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and come back in the top-level context, without their rate."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"url":"\/documentation\/sessions","abstract":[],"title":"Sessions","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"title":"Trackers","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","url":"\/documentation\/trackers","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","title":"Automatic Tracking","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"topic","title":"Consent Gating"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","title":"Defining Events","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"}}}